.It Fl mfunction-return Ns = Ns Ar choice
With
.Cm thunk-extern ,
a function returns by a jump to
.Li __x86_return_thunk ,
which the program supplies, as Linux does; an i386 function that pops a
structure result's hidden pointer takes its return address into
.Li %ecx ,
pops the pointer, and jumps to
.Li __x86_return_thunk_ecx ,
as
.Xr gcc 1 Ns 's
does.
With
.Cm keep ,
the default, it returns by
.Li ret .
.Cm thunk
and
.Cm thunk-inline
are refused.
