from the guard at entry and checked before each return; a changed one
calls
.Fn __stack_chk_fail .
Which functions, as with
.Xr gcc 1 :
.Fl fstack-protector
those with a
.Ic char
array of 8 bytes or more, or one in an aggregate, and those calling
.Fn alloca
or with a variable-length array;
.Fl fstack-protector-strong
those too with any array or aggregate, or a local whose address is
taken;
.Fl fstack-protector-all
